        "original_id": "cd828f60-cbd6-52a3-ac8f-a88da2bc11a5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Crusades\n- People: Cecil B. DeMille, Loretta Young, Henry Wilcoxon\n- Companies: Paramount Pictures\n- Roles: Berengaria of Navarre, Richard I of England\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Actress, Oscar nomination\n\nFacts:\n- The Crusades is a 1935 American historical adventure film produced and directed by Cecil B. DeMille and originally released by Paramount Pictures.\n- In The Crusades, Loretta Young starred as Berengaria of Navarre and Henry Wilcoxon starred as Richard I of England.\n- Loretta Young was an American actress and singer who was born on January 6, 1913, and died on August 12, 2000.\n- Loretta Young won the 1948 Academy Award for Best Actress for her role in the 1947 film The Farmer's Daughter.\n- Loretta Young received an Oscar nomination in 1949 for her role in Come to the Stable.",
